I have identified and resolved the issue according to the requirements:

1. **Root Cause**: In [`Complex.add(Complex rhs)`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/math_53_group_c_fix/src/main/java/org/apache/commons/math/complex/Complex.java#L150-L157), the method did not check whether `this.isNaN` or `rhs.isNaN` was true before performing component addition. Consequently, adding a complex number with a `NaN` imaginary part to a finite real part produced a `Complex` object with a finite real part instead of `Complex.NaN`.
2. **Fix**: Added a check in `Complex.add(Complex rhs)`:
   ```java
   if (isNaN || rhs.isNaN) {
       return NaN;
   }
   ```
3. **Patch**: Generated [`negative_fix.patch`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/math_53_group_c_fix/negative_fix.patch) containing only the changes to `src/main/java/org/apache/commons/math/complex/Complex.java`.
